<title>FINLAND: Finnish EMU opponents increase lead in new poll.</title>
<headline>Finnish EMU opponents increase lead in new poll.</headline>
<dateline>HELSINKI 1997-04-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>More Finns were opposed to membership of European economic and monetary union (EMU) in February-March than a month earlier, Finnish media reported on Thursday.</p>
<p>An opinion survey among slightly over 2,000 people by polling institute Taloustutkimus Oy found opposition rising to 46 percent from 41 percent, and support fell to 36 percent from 38 percent. The rest were undecided.</p>
<p>--Helsinki newsroom +358-9-680 50 245, e-mail news@reuters.fi</p>
</text>
